/*!
    \qmlmodule GameMngr
    \title GameMngr QML Module
    \brief The installed game: launching it, its version and disabled mods.
*/

/*!
    \qmltype GameMngr
    \nativetype vsmm::GameMngr
    \inqmlmodule GameMngr
    \brief Launches the game and reads its version and disabled mods.

    GameMngr reads the game's \c clientsettings.json from
    \l {pathSettings::gameConfig}{Config.paths.gameConfig} and watches it
    for changes.

    \qml
    Button {
        text: qsTr("Launch Game")
        onClicked: GameMngr.launchGame()
    }
    \endqml

    \qml
    Label {
        text: GameMngr.gameVersion ? qsTr("Vintage Story %1").arg(GameMngr.gameVersion)
                                   : qsTr("Game version unknown")
    }
    \endqml
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty string GameMngr::gameVersion
    \readonly
    Installed game version, for example \c 1.21.0, or an empty string when
    unknown.

    The version is read by running the game executable. The first read
    happens during startup, after the main QML file loads and before the
    event loop starts, and blocks for up to three seconds. It
    is read again in the background whenever
    \l {pathSettings::gameExe}{Config.paths.gameExe} changes, and becomes
    empty when a read fails or times out. Update detection is off while it is
    empty, so bind to the property instead of reading it once.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty list<string> GameMngr::disabledMods
    \readonly
    Ids of the mods disabled in the game's \c clientsettings.json.
*/

/*!
    \qmlmethod void GameMngr::launchGame()
    Starts the executable from \l {pathSettings::gameExe}{Config.paths.gameExe}
    as a detached process.
*/

/*!
    \qmlmethod void GameMngr::addDisabledMod(string modId, string version)
    Disables the mod \a modId in \c clientsettings.json, stored there as
    \c {modId@version} with \a version.
*/

/*!
    \qmlmethod void GameMngr::removeDisabledMod(string modId)
    Enables the mod \a modId again by removing every disabled entry with this
    id from \c clientsettings.json.
*/

/*!
    \qmlmodule ModLoader
    \title ModLoader QML Module
    \brief Reads mod zips into the store.
*/

/*!
    \qmltype ModLoader
    \nativetype vsmm::ModLoader
    \inqmlmodule ModLoader
    \brief Reads mod zips and adds them to the store.

    ModLoader runs the startup scan and installs downloaded updates on its
    own. From QML it reads a mod zip without installing it, or installs one:

    \qml
    FileDialog {
        onAccepted: {
            const info = ModLoader.readLocalInfo(selectedFile)
            if (info.error === "")
                ModLoader.load(selectedFile)
        }
    }
    \endqml
*/

/*!
    \qmlmethod localModInfo ModLoader::readLocalInfo(url filePath)
    Reads \c modinfo.json from the zip at \a filePath and returns it without
    installing anything. Runs on the calling thread.

    When the zip or its \c modinfo.json cannot be read, the result has only
    \l {localModInfo::error}{error} set.
*/

/*!
    \qmlmethod void ModLoader::load(url filePath)
    Reads \c modinfo.json from the zip at \a filePath on a worker thread and
    installs the zip into the mods folder. When the mod id is already
    installed, the call counts as an update: the zip is copied next to the
    installed one, and the old zip is moved to the trash when
    \l {generalSettings::deleteOldModVersion}{deleteOldModVersion} is \c true.

    Nothing is reported back to QML. A file that is not a readable mod zip,
    or a version that is not newer than the installed one, is only logged.
*/

/*!
    \qmlvaluetype localModInfo
    \nativetype vsmm::ModLocalInfo
    \inqmlmodule ModLoader
    \brief Contents of a mod zip's \c modinfo.json, returned by \l {ModLoader::readLocalInfo()}{ModLoader.readLocalInfo()}.

    Check \l error first. When it is not empty, the zip could not be read and
    the other members hold their defaults.

    \qml
    FileDialog {
        onAccepted: {
            const info = ModLoader.readLocalInfo(selectedFile)
            if (info.error === "")
                console.log(info.name, info.version, info.authors.join(", "))
        }
    }
    \endqml
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty string localModInfo::id
    Mod id.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty string localModInfo::name
    Display name.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty string localModInfo::version
    \readonly
    Mod version.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty list<string> localModInfo::authors
    Authors, \c ["Unknown"] when \c modinfo.json lists none.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty string localModInfo::description
    Description, \c None when \c modinfo.json has none.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty string localModInfo::side
    Side the mod runs on, \c Unknown when \c modinfo.json has none.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty list<string> localModInfo::dependencies
    Dependencies as \c {modId@version}, with \c * as the version when
    \c modinfo.json leaves it empty.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty string localModInfo::error
    Why the zip could not be read, empty on success.
*/
